;;;
;;; In a rule's `:match` the call is refused at load, *a std.macro pattern macro
;;; used without importing it*, since unexpanded it would never match. A goal is a
;;; premise: refused at load, one line, on every command (exit 1, `ein test`: 2).
;;;
